{
  "id": "hydrostatic_pressure_vs__depth",
  "title": "Hydrostatic Pressure vs. Depth",
  "description": "Calculate hydrostatic pressure in a liquid based on depth using the formula p = ρ g h, where ρ is density, g is acceleration of gravity, and h is the height of fluid column or depth.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Hydrostatic Pressure vs. Depth\n\nHydrostatic pressure in a liquid can be calculated as:\n\n**p = ρ g h**\n\nWhere:\n- **p** = pressure in liquid (N/m², Pa, lbf/ft², psf)\n- **ρ** = density of liquid (kg/m³, slugs/ft³)\n- **g** = acceleration of gravity (9.81 m/s², 32.17405 ft/s²)\n- **h** = height of fluid column or depth in the fluid where pressure is measured (m, ft)\n\nFor water at 4°C with a density of 1000 kg/m³, the hydrostatic pressure increases linearly with depth."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "density",
          "label": "Density (ρ)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1000,
          "unit": "kg/m³"
        },
        {
          "id": "gravity",
          "label": "Acceleration of Gravity (g)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 9.81,
          "unit": "m/s²"
        },
        {
          "id": "depth",
          "label": "Depth (h)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1,
          "unit": "m"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "pressure_pa",
          "label": "Pressure (Pa)",
          "formula": "inputs.density * inputs.gravity * inputs.depth",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_kpa",
          "label": "Pressure (kPa)",
          "formula": "(inputs.density * inputs.gravity * inputs.depth) / 1000",
          "unit": "kPa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_bar",
          "label": "Pressure (bar)",
          "formula": "(inputs.density * inputs.gravity * inputs.depth) / 100000",
          "unit": "bar",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_psi",
          "label": "Pressure (psi)",
          "formula": "(inputs.density * inputs.gravity * inputs.depth) * 0.0001450377",
          "unit": "psi",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
